  "title": "Agroforestry: agriculture of the future? The case of Montpellier",
  "summary": "In Montpellier (France), the SAFE (Silvoarable Agroforestry for Europe) project supports an agroforesty scheme designed to make agricultural systems more resilient to the effects of climate change. Agroforestry can reduce vulnerability, and create potential socio-economic and environmental gains. The agriculture sector in Montpellier is highly vulnerable to higher temperature and more frequent droughts associated with projected climate change. To prepare for the effects of climate change it is important that agriculture in Montpellier takes appropriate adaptation measures.",
